DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270510
SUMMARY:Mother's Day
DESCRIPTION:Mother's Day falls on the second Sunday in May\, a date Congres
 s fixed in 1914\, and it was the work of one woman who spent much of the r
 est of her life objecting to what it became. Anna Jarvis built it as a mem
 orial to her own mother and insisted on the singular possessive: one mothe
 r\, your mother\, not a general tribute to motherhood. The apostrophe held
 . Almost nothing else she wanted did.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holid
 ay/mothers-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/mothers-day/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
